From 27625a3b7212417935755298767a48e5057718ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: topiceyes <273286342+topiceyes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:45:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Make DingTalk OAuth redirect_uri follow the requesting
 host

SERVICE_URL is a single global value, but a deployment can be reachable
through several hostnames (intranet domain + external domain via a cloud
reverse proxy). The OAuth state lives in the session cookie, which is
host-scoped: users starting from another entry were redirected back to
the SERVICE_URL host, where their session (and state) did not exist ->
invalid state / unreachable host.

Build redirect_uri from request.scheme + request.get_host() instead, so
the callback always lands on the entry the user started from. The final
redirect after login is already a relative path, so users stay on their
entry throughout. Register every entry's callback URL in the DingTalk
console (it accepts multiple, comma-separated).

Host is already validated by ALLOWED_HOSTS, so this adds no open
redirect; scheme comes from the usual SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER chain
(upstream proxies must pass the correct X-Forwarded-Proto).

Also reword the 'invalid state' error: host/SERVICE_URL mismatch is no
longer a possible cause.
